FILE: app/src/orbit-camera.ts
```ts
import { createArcRotateCamera, attachControl, enableArcRotateKeyboardControls } from "@babylonjs/lite";
import type { ArcRotateCamera, SceneContext } from "@babylonjs/lite";

export function createOrbitCamera(canvas: HTMLCanvasElement, scene: SceneContext): ArcRotateCamera {
    enableArcRotateKeyboardControls();
    const camera = createArcRotateCamera(0, Math.PI / 4, 10, { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 });
    attachControl(camera, canvas, scene, { keyboard: true });
    return camera;
}
```

I created `src/orbit-camera.ts` which calls `enableArcRotateKeyboardControls()` (required before `keyboard: true` is honoured, per note 10), builds an `ArcRotateCamera` at radius 10 looking at the origin with a sensible 45°-from-pole starting angle, and attaches the standard pointer/touch controls plus keyboard via `attachControl`. The only thing I was slightly unsure of is whether `SceneContext` and `ArcRotateCamera` are re-exported from the root `"@babylonjs/lite"` entry point or only from sub-paths; I assumed a flat export since you said the library is imported as that single specifier.
